{
  "dom_id": "step-q165773",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A committee will be randomly formed of $4$ people selected from a pool of $18$ candidates consisting of $10$ men and $8$ women. What is the probability that the committee consists of $2$ men and $2$ women? Round your answer to the nearest percent.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ represent the event described in the question. Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =\\frac{n}{N},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N$ is the total number of ways to pick $4$ people out of $18,$ and $n$ is the number of picks where $2$ are men and $2$ are women.\n\nSince the order in which people will be chosen does not matter, we use combinations. \n\nFirst, we compute $N.$ The number of ways to pick $4$ people from a total of $18$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N={}_{18}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{18!}{4!\\cdot 14!}=3\\,060.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $n.$ The computation of $n$ can be divided into two steps: \n\n- the number of ways to choose $2$ (out of $8$) women is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{8}{C}_{2}=\\frac{8!}{2!\\cdot 6!}=28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the number of ways to choose $2$ (out of $10$) men is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{C}_{2} & =\\frac{10!}{2!\\cdot 8!}=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the results from the above steps, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n={}_{8}{C}_{2}\\cdot {}_{10}{C}_{2}=28\\cdot 45=1\\,260.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =\\frac{1\\,260}{3\\,060}=\\frac{7}{17}≈0.41=41%.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
